{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/398203-what-does-the-goblin-marchant-know","id":398203,"title":"What does the Goblin Marchant know?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-08T17:15:48-08:00","id":398203,"title":"What does the Goblin Marchant know?","content":"My player has come in to deal with local Goblin Merchant ( only one, for now ) to provide him certain &quot;products&quot; in exchange for Tokens and information. Question is: <b>How much the Goblin will know about Faerie world?</b><br /> <br /> 1. The PC bring him unknown Token - the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnival_of_Venice#Carnival_masks\" target=\"_blank\">Venetian Mask</a> that makes inner Mask of changeling automatic strengthen ( like with spending Glamour, but for free ), even without the different shadow problem. Could Merchant just say what it it on first look? Does they have &quot;Identify Item&quot; spell on them? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know the Lost just can feel the item is Token with Wits+Wyrd, but they do not know how exactly it works till they try. Could Goblin just look on it and know it's properties?<br /> <br /> 2. The same PC has unclear visions of Spring Court symbology - renewal, Emerald, animals like fox and rabbit - does the Goblins know about Court systems in any length, to make hints for PC about it? Or are they totally in their own business, and do not know about changelings life on Earth, in general?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T20:30:02-08:00","id":398335,"title":"","content":"How much a Goblin Merchant knows about things depends on the merchant, really. Is it a young up-and-comer with more verve than experience? An old-timer with several laps of the Hedge under its belt? <br /> <br /> 1: There are Contracts that let a Changeling know precisely what the properties of a magical item are. It'd be fair to let a Goblin merchant have a similar Contract, especially if that merchant buys and sells mystical baubles and gewgaws often. Otherwise, it might be able to use common sense and experience to suss out some of the truth. <br /> <br /> 2: Again, this depends in great part on the Goblin in question. If the Goblin is well-traveled or if the Courts have had a presence in the area within the Goblin's lifetime (and remember that Goblins aren't human, and may have mayflower lives or may live centuries), then it might well have seen such Court symbology from other Lost and learnt what it means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T08:24:26-08:00","id":398783,"title":"","content":"1) In my games I give each goblin merchant a specialty of some kind. How well they can identify a token or other item a changeling brings in trade depends on whether or not it's in the goblin's wheelhouse. For example, one of my more popular merchants from my last CtL game dealt in bodies of all kinds from corpses to living breathing animals. He could recognize pretty much any part of any animal and use them to create the transplants and frankensteinian monsters he sold. Bring him a token and he'd have questions about it's functionality. He might not even take it as payment if he thought the character's worn't being honest about it's powers or drawbacks.<br /> <br /> 2) I like to emphasize the strangeness of goblins. Part of how I did this was by ensuring that they have their own world that they understand and that they don't generally know much about the life changelings lead outside the market. Mind you, if we're just talking about basic symbology the merchant might make the link to the mantles he's seen on changelings at the market and ID Spring that way. If the symbology refers to anything deeper than that I'd have the merchant, at best, send the characters to a knowledgeable changeling or even misdirect them with a (unintentional) red-herring like the Wineberry Cross from Dancers in the Dusk (pg 90).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4692-helel","name":"helel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}